{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788269387,"nonce":"jycwfns1P4n4QJ8QAJEOLUsWlm4=","message":"TWO CORRECTIONS AND ONE OWNERSHIP CALL, from the verify-first pass of the round\nthat makes blueprints buildable, 2026-09-01. Both corrections are to the round's\nown brief, not to this issue — recorded here because this is the issue that acts\non them.\n\n\nThe round's brief said `templates/power-room.ir.json` exists \"and the rest are\n.md only, so establish whether IR is a format or one example\". That question is\nalready answered and does not need a session:\n\n    templates/bedroom.ir.json           size [5,7]\n    templates/freezer-kitchen.ir.json   size [11,6]\n    templates/power-room.ir.json        size [7,7]\n\nAll three exist, all three carry the identical nine-key dialect —\n`defName, size, layers, terrain, roof, extension, modRequirements,\nspawnConduits, animalCells` — and the footprints match `INDEX.md`'s table\nexactly. Every template is the pair `INDEX.md` describes (\"a patch that touches\none half touches both or it is not done\"). The corpus is conformant; it is just\nnot MODULAR, which is this issue's actual complaint and is unaffected.\n\nPractical consequence: re-cutting to 7x7 is an edit to three conforming\ndocuments in a settled dialect, not a format design exercise.\n\n\n`INDEX.md`, verbatim: **\"Row 0 = north is PROPOSED, not established — 3.3 pins\nit.\"** Comment #2 above already flags this (\"a grid makes that pin urgent, since\nphase is meaningless without a fixed orientation\") and it remains unpinned.\n\nIt is not cosmetic. `INDEX.md` records the mechanism: `Building_Cooler.TickRare`\ncools `Position + IntVec3.South.RotatedBy(Rotation)` and vents to\n`Position + IntVec3.North.RotatedBy(Rotation)`, so `freezer-kitchen`'s two\n`Cooler_North` cells in row 0 chill row 1 **only if row 0 is north**. Pin it\nsouth and that template heats its own freezer. Until it is pinned, each\ntemplate's .md prose is normative and says which way it assumed — which is a\ncorpus that cannot be machine-consumed.\n\nAlso worth knowing before pinning: the two artifacts disagree today and neither\nis wrong on its own terms. `baseviz/ir.py`'s docstring says only \"row 0 is the\ntop row as written in the XML\" — an XML-order statement that takes no compass\nposition. `baseviz/render.py` says \"Planes are north-up row-major: row 0 is\nz = oz + h - 1\" — but that is the map-DUMP renderer, a different artifact. The\nmod agrees with render.py where it speaks at all: `CropRenderer.Render` walks\n`for (int z = rect.maxZ; z \u003e= rect.minZ; z--)` and comments\n`rows[0] is z = origin_z + h - 1 (north at top)`. So north-up is the established\nconvention in two of three places and merely unstated in `ir.py`.\n\n\n`INDEX.md` assigns the pin to 3.3 (`1adc737`). The current round moves it here,\nand the reason is which files the work touches:\n\n- The pin is a decision about `templates/` and `baseviz/`. Neither is C#.\n- The mod has **no opinion on IR orientation at all** — it never reads a\n  template; `place-layout` would be its first consumer and does not exist.\n- 3.3's session in this round is serialized behind the shared site routine\n  because `Source/AutoRimmer/` produces one DLL. This issue's session is not,\n  and runs in parallel.\n\nSo: pin **row 0 = north** here, record it in DESIGN's decisions log with the\n`Building_Cooler` reasoning, state it in `ir.py`'s docstring so the format\ndeclares its own orientation, and comment the result onto `1adc737`. That\ndischarges `INDEX.md`'s open point and makes module phase well-defined, which is\nthe precondition for everything else on this issue.\n\nSequencing from comment #1 is unchanged and not being reopened: 3.3's `build`\nstill goes first. The pin is not the grid — it is the coordinate system the grid\nneeds in order to be stated at all, and it costs nothing to settle now.","files":null}]}